From f6ed2ea927a2f4faacbc855941b87348e6092075 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 14:19:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 302/307] !B (Sandbox) Use one stable composite order for plate
 colour, preview to stamp.

The live preview composited overlapping colour plates in entity-iterator order,
i.e. spawn order, which is not reproducible across a save and reload; the export
inherited it; and Stamp Colour walked the selection in whatever order the
selection happened to be in. Three tiers, three orders, so two plates that share
ground could stamp in the opposite order to the one shown.

There is now one order, and it is deliberately the height bake's:
Bake Priority ascending, entity GUID as the tie-break
(CTerrainPlateComponent::BakesBefore), so plate colour stacks the way plate
relief does. ITerrainPlateCommit::GetCommitOrderPriority exposes it,
TerrainPlateColourOverlay::CompositesBefore is the single comparator, ScanPlates
sorts the preview and the export snapshots, and the colour stamp sorts the
selection. Because each plate is written into CRGBLayer over what the previous
one already wrote, walking the selection lowest-first reproduces the preview's
stack texel for texel.

The one case that cannot be fixed by ordering: an unselected plate that is still
drawing live and composites UNDER a stamped plate. A stamped plate's colour
becomes part of the ground, which is the bottom of the stack, so that plate now
draws over it and the two swap places in the shared rim. Compositing it into the
tiles as well was considered and rejected - it would then be blended twice, once
in the ground and once live, which puts it on top anyway and tightens its rim
(the effect GetLiveColourState stands down for). It is named instead, in a
warning that says to select both and stamp them together. An unselected plate
that composites ABOVE the stamped one is unaffected and is not warned about: it
drew last before and it draws last now.

Alternatives in scene-notes/decisions/terrain-plate-colour-stamp-order.md.
